{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfScpzf3xH4uHHRHiE6hP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I have a clear picture of the codebase:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model (Order.kt:11-16): currently has no status field\n- Shipment model (Shipment.kt:9-14): already has status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt): POST create and GET endpoints exist\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt): POST create and GET endpoints\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27): in-memory ConcurrentHashMap store\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27): in-memory ConcurrentHashMap store\n- Error handling (ApiExceptions.kt, GlobalExceptionHandler.kt): centralized via ApiException subclasses\n- Error codes (ApiError.kt:31-37): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Errors thrown as ResourceNotFoundException (404) or ConflictException (409)\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on both status and error envelope structure\n- Controllers are simple, repositories are in-memory, error handling is centralized\n- Data models are Kotlin data classes\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - must add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. OrderController.kt - must add cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - must add method to find shipments by orderId\n4. ShipmentController.kt - must check order status before creating shipment\n5. ApiError.kt - must add ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt - must add tests for cancel scenarios\n7. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - must add tests for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Atomicity: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, cancel must fail with no changes\n- Existing tests must pass\n- Backward compatibility for order creation\n\n**Open questions:** None - requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order; create OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values; update OrderController's create to set status = ACTIVE\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order, throws 404 if missing\n   - Checks if any shipment is CONFIRMED - if yes, throw 409 (no changes)\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments, sets order status to CANCELLED\n   - If already CANCELLED, succeed without changes\n   - Returns the updated order with 200 status\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: In create method, check if order exists and is CANCELLED - if yes, throw 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code; if order doesn't exist, proceed as before\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to enum\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancel ACTIVE order succeeds, shipments are cancelled\n   - Cancel already CANCELLED order succeeds with no changes\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment fails 409, nothing changes\n   - Cancel nonexistent order returns 404\n   - Response body format is correct\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409\n   - Creating shipment for non-existent order still works (current behavior)\n\n**Alternative rejected:** I considered making cancel operation update shipment status directly without fetching them, but iterating and updating each shipment individually is clearer and allows the atomicity check (verify all before updating any).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments:*\n- Input: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Read: order from repository, all shipments for that order\n- Check: if any CONFIRMED shipment exists → throw ConflictException with 409\n- Write: order.status = CANCELLED, each CREATED shipment.status = CANCELLED\n- Return: updated order with 200 OK\n\n*Cancel already CANCELLED order:*\n- Read: order from repository\n- Check: order.status == CANCELLED\n- Action: succeed without changes\n- Return: order unchanged with 200 OK\n\n*Cancel nonexistent order:*\n- Read: order not found\n- Throw: ResourceNotFoundException with 404\n\n*Create shipment for CANCELLED order:*\n- Read: order from repository\n- Check: order.status == CANCELLED\n- Throw: ConflictException with 409 using ORDER_CANCELLED code\n- Return: error envelope\n\n*Create shipment for nonexistent order:*\n- Read: order not found\n- Action: proceed (current behavior, no order existence check)\n- Create: shipment\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nNew tests in OrderControllerTest:\n1. `cancelsAnActiveOrder()` - cancel ACTIVE order, verify status CANCELLED, verify shipments cancelled\n2. `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrder()` - cancel CANCELLED order, verify succeeds with no changes\n3. `cancelWithConfirmedShipment()` - cancel with CONFIRMED shipment, verify 409 and nothing changes\n4. `cancelNonexistentOrder()` - cancel missing order, verify 404\n\nNew tests in ShipmentControllerTest:\n1. `rejectShipmentForCancelledOrder()` - create shipment for CANCELLED order, verify 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n2. `allowShipmentForNonexistentOrder()` - create shipment for missing order, verify current behavior (allowed)\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with the Order model:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":21514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":833},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8f58657-8fa3-4c00-833d-5d8e