. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added orderRepository injection and check before creating shipment. Prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders while preserving behavior for nonexistent orders.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` error codes. These are part of the API contract now.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 6 new test cases covering all cancel scenarios. Updated reset to clear shipments too.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 2 new test cases for cancelled order rejection and nonexistent order allowance. Updated reset to clear orders too.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. The implementation is complete and all cases specified in the ticket are handled.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint to allow order cancellation with atomic semantics: cancel ACTIVE orders to CANCELLED status (persisting and cancelling CREATED shipments), allow retry on already-CANCELLED orders, fail 409 with no changes if CONFIRMED shipment exists, fail 404 for missing orders, and prevent shipment creation for CANCELLED orders.\n\nChanged       \n- Order.kt: Added status field (OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE/CANCELLED) to track order lifecycle\n- OrderController.kt: Added cancel endpoint with atomic transaction logic (verify CONFIRMED, cancel CREATED shipments, update order status)\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method to support cancellation of shipments\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added order status check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 tests for cancel endpoint (ACTIVE→CANCELLED, already CANCELLED, CONFIRMED shipment blocks, missing order, mixed shipment statuses, and ACTIVE status creation)\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 2 tests for shipment creation validation (rejected for CANCELLED order, allowed for nonexistent order)\n\nTests         \n- `createsAnOrderWithActiveStatus()` - Verifies new orders have ACTIVE status\n- `cancelsAnActiveOrderAndReturnsTheCancelledOrder()` - Verifies cancel endpoint returns CANCELLED order\n- `cancelsCreatedShipmentsWhenCancellingAnOrder()` - Verifies CREATED shipments are cancelled atomically\n- `cancellingAnAlreadyCancelledOrderSucceedsWithoutChanges()` - Verifies retry idempotence\n- `cancellingAnOrderWithConfirmedShipmentFailsWith409()` - Verifies atomic failure with no changes\n- `cancellingANonexistentOrderReturns404()` - Verifies 404 for missing order\n- `cancellingAnOrderWithCancelledShipmentsDoesNotFail()` - Verifies only CREATED shipments are cancelled\n- `rejectShipmentCreationForACancelledOrderWith409()` - Verifies shipment creation blocked for CANCELLED orders\n- `allowsShipmentCreationForANonexistentOrder()` - Verifies backward compatibility (nonexistent order doesn't block shipment)\n\nVerification  Command: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ directory\nResult: BUILD SUCCESS - 22 tests passed (11 OrderControllerTest, 7 ShipmentControllerTest, 3 CustomerControllerTest, 1 application test), 0 failures, 0 errors\n\nNot done      Nothing - all acceptance criteria implemented and verified.","ttft_ms":4248,"type":"result","duration_ms":190086,"uuid":"3154b2a1-e962-4b10-8e41-1aa9f7d233b5","ttft_stream_ms":584,"time_to_request_ms":26,"first_content_frame_ms":584,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

